  "title": "Weakening AI copyright law will spell 'disaster for creativity', global music body warns Albanese",
  "summary": "The Global Phonographic Industry (IFPI) warns that weakening AI copyright law could lead to a 'huge mistake' and damage Australia's reputation, as it watches with concern how the Albanese government responds to big tech demands. While local creatives raise constitutional issues and artists threaten political backlash, the IFPI has expressed worries about Australia potentially agreeing to demands from other nations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Global Phonographic Industry (IFPI) warns that weakening AI copyright law could lead to a 'huge mistake' and damage Australia's reputation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Australia's prime minister, Anthony Albanese, faces concerns about the impact of AI-driven copyright changes on creativity and the potential for political backlash.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The IFPI has raised concerns about Australia agreeing to demands from other nations as the global music industry watches closely.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
